# An allowlist: nothing enters the build context unless the Dockerfile copies it. Allowed are the
# package manifests, the lockfile, tsconfig.base.json and the sources of shared/, server/ and web/.
# Everything else (.git, specs, plans, infra, scripts, e2e, fixtures, local config ...) is out.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.base.json
!shared
!server
!web

# Inside the allowed directories (patterns are matched at every depth). Dependencies and build
# output are produced inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.md

# Secrets and local state must not be copied into the image, and web/.env* would be inlined by
# Vite into the public bundle.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.npmrc
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/credentials*.json
**/*.tfstate*
**/*.tfvars
